{"title":"1977 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of intersection of the diagonals of convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3efd92d7eef6e4b04b61b6ff7e353462a2607585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q,R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the centers of the circles \ncircumscribing triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb94515779fb01f7fd3f79b5d2085d1ee88910bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE, BCE, CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f073f1d4a966b7bd810c64eda9c4609ca45a70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }PQRS\\text{ is a parallelogram}\\\\ \\textbf{(B) }PQRS\\text{ is a parallelogram if an only if }ABCD\\text{ is a rhombus}\\\\ \\textbf{(C) }PQRS\\text{ is a parallelogram if an only if }ABCD\\text{ is a rectangle}\\\\ \\textbf{(D) }PQRS\\text{ is a parallelogram if an only if }ABCD\\text{ is a parallelogram}\\\\ \\textbf{(E) }\\text{none of the above are true}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"514\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2bcc4fbcb6dd28f70ea584900c95e658c7efea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db06268e8eb838b6fa78ca2be74897835cf3a004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> be the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d6376813e82e214b6c6331fd6ac90dd0434c991b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = l_1 \\cap l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab3b379200ef7e7f1fcdea6e565142cc77a8d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = l_2 \\cap l_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a0f8dc6b07e2c65af4991cad77c079b0bd34db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = l_3 \\cap l_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2a8a6c1c9a06719ee1f5cb9cc47422ae9e1677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = l_4 \\cap l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" />.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c27f5fa843c206e8bb744299f95a7b1ac8769c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1 = \\overleftrightarrow{PS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a8551286629d52898503127ab20140385ab470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2 = \\overleftrightarrow{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecce99526936184a2bb471211ecb9ce28df39e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_3 = \\overleftrightarrow{QR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"24\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e4503deb3b8f80d4757cf98f675335d24bb7d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_4 = \\overleftrightarrow{RS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"24\" />.  \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2131518c8ab626f614f0ac0255f353c41a5f68d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{PS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265d561ecbcc61507cee8894107816a739ac326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{QR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" /> are both perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9627dc495e65b51d79abccbeb3356141b51c3147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{AC}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"22\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83fee64b5a39299fc3957089217af2994583500c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{PS} \\parallel \\overleftrightarrow{QR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.  Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec9e6f5defd1ee1b0c3f2ebc143ef40d89091dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f80fe6852dc3ee008cc59fbfa03c03840a3c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{RS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"21\" /> are both perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eed62ba63a5367b1b32e3e62339b9f8d66a6980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"21\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f175a69a0ec760467d0ece9abfc516799799058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{PQ} \\parallel \\overleftrightarrow{RS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> has two pairs of parallel opposite sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81ad5eea70a52285a73101d96f53f5fa2d083b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }PQRS\\text{ is a parallelogram}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"238\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805452ee372321839953fbd750cd9b23b973a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> respectively. Since the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a> of a triangle is determined by the intersection of its perpendicular bisectors, each of the pairs mentioned earlier are perpendicular to each other. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8ce413185cb7f9ddec132453f2addca76e676c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle SPQ=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11fca6ada2ecac6f85cd7f74c5b22137044b041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle LEM=180^\\circ-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"151\" height=\"13\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39ac15038ae16427c8116059389ea5c64d4967b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PLC=PMD=90^\\circ$\" width=\"175\" height=\"13\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9d471684b49680f1f57ea3eb9bc4b630665e3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEC=180^\\circ-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />, which similarly implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4f95dc7242401046241c3ff62fabaeeb243077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QRS=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />. Through a similar method, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d68910de6269356322f5fd8bddb1115ea1f9317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PSR=\\angle PQR=180^\\circ-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"225\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since the opposite angles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> are congruent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is indeed a parallelogram - and we showed this without any assumption about the type of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> was. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is always a parallelogram, and so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME\" title=\"1977 AHSME\">1977 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1977 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1977 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1977\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1977 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1977 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME